ype\":\"function\",\"name\":\"SPOKE_CONFIGURATOR_ROLE\",\"inputs\":[],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"uint64\",\"internalType\":\"uint64\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"function\",\"name\":\"SPOKE_DOMAIN_ADMIN_ROLE\",\"inputs\":[],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"uint64\",\"internalType\":\"uint64\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"function\",\"name\":\"SPOKE_USER_POSITION_UPDATER_ROLE\",\"inputs\":[],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"uint64\",\"internalType\":\"uint64\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{},\"author\":\"Aave Labs\",\"title\":\"Roles library\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{},\"notice\":\"Defines the different roles used by the protocol and their target selectors. Role IDs are namespaced by domain:   - AccessManager:     0 (default admin)   - Hub:               100-199   - HubConfigurator:   200-299   - Spoke:             300-399   - SpokeConfigurator: 400-499 ## Role strategy A single authority contract will be used to manage the roles for all applicable contracts on a given chain. Role IDs, selector mappings, and overall configuration should be kept identical across chains to avoid additional overhead and role divergence. Hub and Spoke roles remain granular (e.g. HUB_CONFIGURATOR_ROLE, HUB_FEE_MINTER_ROLE, HUB_DEFICIT_ELIMINATOR_ROLE each control a distinct set of selectors). HubConfigurator and SpokeConfigurator follow a different approach: initially, a single Domain Admin role per domain (HUB_CONFIGURATOR_DOMAIN_ADMIN_ROLE = 200, SPOKE_CONFIGURATOR_DOMAIN_ADMIN_ROLE = 400) holds all target selectors. As more granular roles are introduced, they are added at the next available ID (201, 202, ... / 401, 402, ...) and the corresponding selectors are reassigned from the Domain Admin role to the new granular role:   - Existing role IDs should never be overwritten or reused for a different purpose.   - New roles are always appended with an incremented ID.   - The Domain Admin role (200/400) only ever has its selector set shrink over     time as selectors are divided into more granular roles.   - Addresses holding the Domain Admin role should be granted the new     granular role to retain their existing access.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"lib/crane/contracts/protocols/lending/aave/v4/deployments/utils/libraries/Roles.sol\":\"Roles\"},\"evmVersion\":\"osaka\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"@battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/src/\",\"@crane/=lib/crane/\",\"@matterlabs/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/lib/\",\"@nomicfoundation/=node_modules/@nomicfoundation/\",\"@opengsn/=node_modules/@opengsn/\",\"@openzeppelin/=node_modules/@openzeppelin/\",\"@oz/=lib/crane/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\"@ozu/=lib/crane/contracts/external/openzeppelin-upgradeable/\",\"battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/\",\"battlechain-lib-mocks/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/test/mocks/\",\"battlechain-lib/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/src/\",\"battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/\",\"chainlink-ccip/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/vendor/optimism/interop-lib/v0/src/\",\"chainlink-evm/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-evm/\",\"chainlink-local/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/src/\",\"clones/=lib/crane/contracts/external/clones-with-immutable-args/\",\"contracts/external/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/=lib/crane/contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/\",\"contracts/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"crane/